      "role": "user",
      "content": "{\"objective\":\"Rank candidates for experimental investigation of MSA-conformer preference. Integrate geometry and sequence-structure evidence; retain sequence and epitope diversity among supported candidates.\",\"targets\":{\"MSA\":[\"6XYO\",\"6XYP\",\"6XYQ\"],\"controls\":[\"8A9L\",\"6CU7\"]},\"pose_columns\":[\"repeat\",\"contacts_per_residue\",\"clashes_per_residue\",\"assembly_clashes_per_residue\",\"polar_pairs_per_residue\",\"opposite_charge_pairs_per_residue\",\"receptor_backbone_rmsd_a\",\"peptide_cn_max_deviation_a\",\"geometry_eligible\",\"complex_nll\",\"complex_nll_sd\",\"peptide_only_nll\",\"context_gain\",\"context_gain_sd\"],\"chemistry_columns\":[\"length\",\"gravy\",\"hydrophobic_run\"],\"geometry_rules\":[\"contacts_per_residue counts distinct peptide/central-receptor residue pairs within 4.5 A / peptide length.\",\"clashes_per_residue and assembly_clashes_per_residue count heavy-atom pairs below 2 A / peptide length.\",\"geometry_eligible uses zero central and assembly clashes plus peptide C-N maximum deviation <=0.3 A from approximate 1.33 A; this is a permissive structural eligibility rule, with detailed metrics retained.\",\"polar_pairs_per_residue counts N/O proximity below 3.5 A; opposite_charge_pairs_per_residue counts D/E vs K/R atom proximity below 4.5 A. These are geometric proxies.\",\"receptor_backbone_rmsd_a measures target C-alpha displacement from experimental coordinates without alignment. Large displacement reduces support.\",\"Use all available poses. Two poses provide limited repeatability evidence; one leaves repeatability less established.\"],\"inverse_rules\":[\"ProteinMPNN evaluates the original peptide sequence, with receptor chains fixed; complex_nll is averaged over peptide residues and eight decoding orders. Lower means greater sequence-backbone compatibility.\",\"peptide_only_nll evaluates the exact same peptide backbone with target chains removed. context_gain=peptide_only_nll-complex_nll; higher means greater model support from the target environment. Both contexts use matched peptide decoding orders.\",\"These quantities are model evidence for sequence-structure compatibility and context dependence. They are proxies; affinity and selectivity require measured labels.\",\"Compare the same peptide across the three MSA conformers and BOTH controls. Favor broad, repeatable MSA support; a credible strongly compatible control reduces discrimination support.\",\"Null inverse values mark geometrically ineligible poses. Such control observations leave control compatibility unknown. Target distortion and sampling sensitivity reduce confidence.\",\"Peptide-only correction addresses backbone/composition preference partially; graph changes and shared training biases remain. Interpret small gaps against decoding-order variation and independent-pose variation.\"],\"instructions\":\"Assign all required candidate keys a 0-100 relative experimental priority. Larger values indicate earlier priority. Interpret incomplete evidence as uncertainty. Write decision_logic and final support/limitation in concise Simplified Chinese accessible to an AI researcher. Distinguish reliable local compatibility from disease selectivity. Cite actual numerical observations in final explanations.\",\"candidates\":[{\"id\":\"C000\",\"site\":\"site_2\",\"sequence\":\"RFSPGQEVTRSN\",\"chemistry\":[12,-1.4,1],\"poses\":{\"6XYO\":[[1,1.083,0.0,0.0,0.333,0.0,0.201,0.025,true,3.35724,0.03263,3.28133,-0.07591,0.05207],[2,1.083,1.833,6.75,0.25,0.083,0.009,3.47,false,null,null,null,null,null]],\"6XYP\":[[1,0.417,0.0,0.667,0.25,0.0,0.202,0.028,false,null,null,null,null,null],[2,0.333,0.0,0.0,0.333,0.417,0.204,0.032,true,3.37852,0.02507,3.15396,-0.22456,0.02431]],\"6XYQ\":[[1,0.75,0.0,0.0,0.5,0.167,0.203,0.029,true,2.85164,0.02301,2.96848,0.11684,0.01893],[2,0.833,0.0,0.0,0.333,0.25,0.201,0.028,true,3.03695,0.02482,2.84136,-0.19559,0.03116]],\"8A9L\":[[1,0.833,0.0,0.0,0.667,0.083,0.209,0.045,true,3.32869,0.031